  "result": "I fixed the bug, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` now gives 45 passed, 2 skipped.\n\n- **Fix:** In `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py`), `bound - dir` became `bound + dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` when clamping up to `min` and `dir=-1` when clamping down to `max`, so an open bound has to move by `+dir`. `click.IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True).convert('0', None, None)` now returns 1.\n- **Tests:** I added four cases to the clamp parametrize list at the top of `tests/test_types.py`:\n  - `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"0\"` gives 1 (the case you reported).\n  - The same range with `\"-5\"` gives 1.\n  - `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"5\"` gives 4.\n  - The same range with `\"9\"` gives 4.\n\nI did not run the old code against the new cases to confirm they fail without the fix.",
